<title>TAIWAN: CPC offered $80 mln for Emirates oil stake - agency.</title>
<headline>CPC offered $80 mln for Emirates oil stake - agency.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp has offered about US$80 million to Crescent Oil Co of the United Arab Emirates for a 40 percent stake in a Crescent affiliate called BGOI, state-funded news agency reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The Central News Agency, without identifying its sources, said the acquisition would allow Chinese Petroleum to take part in BGOI's oil exploration programmes and operations of the firm's existing oil fields.</p>
</text>
